## 11. AUTOMATIC COUPON AFTER AN ELIGIBLE ₹200+ PURCHASE

Implement a promotional coupon programme.

### Eligibility

When a customer's qualifying order has a merchandise subtotal of ₹200 or more, excluding delivery charges and taxes for eligibility purposes, issue one coupon for their next order.

Example:

Customer buys products worth ₹250.

The order qualifies for one coupon.

The coupon can be used on the next eligible order.

**Important:** Calculate eligibility using the configured rule and the backend's verified item totals. Do not allow delivery fees, GST, or manipulated frontend values to make an otherwise ineligible order qualify.

### Coupon properties

Every coupon must contain:
- Unique coupon code
- Customer ID
- Discount type
- Discount value
- Minimum eligible merchandise subtotal
- Creation timestamp
- Expiration timestamp
- Redemption status
- Associated qualifying order
- Associated redemption order, when used

Example code:

`OTS-7K4P9X`

Generate codes securely and enforce uniqueness in the database. The example is illustrative.

### Expiry

Coupons must expire **7 days after their issue timestamp**, using the Asia/Kolkata business time zone for customer-facing dates.

Store timestamps consistently in the backend and enforce expiry on the server.

Example:
- Issued: 23 October 2026, 6:00 PM IST
- Expires: 30 October 2026, 6:00 PM IST

Show the exact expiry date and time on the profile page.

### Coupon redemption rules

- Each coupon belongs to one customer.
- A coupon can be redeemed only once.
- A coupon can only be used by its intended customer.
- Expired coupons cannot be redeemed.
- A coupon cannot be applied to the same order that earned it.
- Apply the coupon to the next eligible order only.
- Validate coupon status and eligibility server-side.
- Prevent two simultaneous requests from redeeming the same coupon twice.
- If the order is cancelled or refunded, apply the configured coupon reversal policy.
- Never silently remove an earned coupon.
- Clearly explain coupon eligibility and exclusions before checkout.

### Discount configuration

Create an admin setting for:
- Fixed discount amount
- Percentage discount
- Minimum order value
- Maximum discount, if applicable
- Coupon validity in days — default 7
- Whether coupons can be combined with other promotions
- Whether the reward applies to dine-in, parcel, or both

Use a configurable sample discount during development, such as ₹20 off a future qualifying order. Mark this as a sample until the owner approves the actual promotion.

### Coupon example

First eligible order:
- Merchandise subtotal: ₹250
- Order is completed.
- System issues one unique coupon.
- Coupon expires after seven days.

Next order:
- Customer signs in.
- Selects their valid coupon.
- Website validates the coupon.
- Bill recalculates with the discount.
- Coupon becomes redeemed only after the order is successfully created and the redemption transaction is committed.

Display messages such as:

“Your next tea break just got better! You've unlocked a special Oru Tea Sollu! coupon.”

“Coupon expires in 5 days.”

“Congratulations on your 50th order! You're one of our valued regulars.”

These messages should only appear when the corresponding reward has genuinely been earned.

